I added `specdojo register branch-push --project <project-id> [--dry-run]`. It covers first-time setup and recovery, so the orchestrator no longer needs to type `git branch`, `git pull --rebase` or `git push`. The new tests (3 unit, 10 integration) and the existing register tests (58) pass. The trial-repository check after integration hasn't been done; it belongs to the orchestrator.

**What the command does**
- **Push target:** it only pushes to the `remote` and `branch` set in `register_sync`. It takes no ref or branch argument, and anything extra (`--branch`, a positional ref) is rejected.
- **Sync not enabled:** it prints why and stops with exit code 1.
- **First time, branch exists nowhere:** it creates the branch from the integration branch (`integration_branch`, default `project/<project-id>/develop`), creates the dedicated worktree in the same place the sync uses, and pushes.
- **Branch only on the remote:** it creates the local branch and worktree and pushes nothing.
- **Branch only local:** it checks it and pushes it as a new remote branch. The ticket didn't cover this case; I chose this behaviour.
- **Recovery:** it continues a stopped rebase, then runs `pull --rebase` and push.
  - If conflicts remain, it lists the files and how to fix them, and stops with exit code 1.
  - It keeps recorded files and local commits.
- **Checks:** before pushing it runs the same checks as `register branch-check`, and pushes nothing if they fail.
- **Locking:** it runs inside the same lock as the sync.
- **`--dry-run`:** it shows the branch it would create, the commits it would push and the check results, and changes nothing.

**Behaviour I decided on (also written in the ticket)**
- `--dry-run` takes no lock and doesn't fetch; it reads the remote tip with `git ls-remote`. It exits 1 if the real run would stop.
- If the worktree has uncommitted changes outside a rebase, it lists them and stops instead of committing them. This avoids publishing, for example, a duplicate claim that the user hasn't decided to keep.
- On the first push, if the integration branch isn't on the remote yet, its commits fail the check. The error message tells you to push the integration branch first.

**Two changes outside the new command**
- **Failure message:** I changed the message shown when a normal sync fails so it points to `register branch-push` instead of manual git commands. The wording the existing tests check is kept, and the sync itself behaves as before. `branch-merge`, `branch-guard` and `branch-check` are untouched.
- **Bug fix:** while a rebase is stopped, the dedicated worktree couldn't be found by branch name, because HEAD is detached. I fixed this in the new command's lookup.

**Validation:** I ran prettier, eslint, `tsc -b`, the two new test files and the whole register test directory, markdownlint on the changed Markdown, and `npm run validate:history-links`. All passed. The parent runner's allowlisted checks were not run here; they run after this stage.

The ticket now has the work table, results, related documents and a "CHANGELOG に書く事項" section with draft Added and Changed lines; `CHANGELOG.md` itself is unchanged.

**Still open**
- The orchestrator still needs to try first-time setup, recovery and `--dry-run` in a temporary repository with a bare remote (work table row 5, left `open`).
- The uncommitted sync-settings changes in `../worktrees/feature-prj-0001-register-sync` and `../worktrees/feature-prj-0002-register-sync` may also describe manual git steps. If so, they should be switched to `register branch-push` there; this task didn't touch them.

Files changed:
- New: `src/register/branch-push.ts`, `tests/src/register/branch-push.test.ts`, `tests/src/register/register-branch-push.integration.test.ts`
- Modified: `src/register/branch-commands.ts`, `src/shared/register-branch.ts`
- Docs: `docs/ja/specdojo/guides/register-operation-guide.md`, `docs/ja/specdojo/references/command-reference.md`, `docs/ja/specdojo/references/specdojo-config-reference.md`
- Ticket: `docs/ja/projects/prj-0001/controls/project-register/pjr-m120-register-branch-push.md`

